    "text": "- Use only standard library. No classes except namedtuple/dataclass if it helps.\n\n<think>\nThe user wants a Python script implementing a speculative decoding acceptance scorer.\nKey requirements:\n1.  `accept_curve(gold, draft, gamma)` function.\n    -   Teacher-forced: `draft[t]` is the token generated by the draft model given `gold[:t]`.\n    -   Speculative decoding rule: The verifier checks `draft[t]`, `draft[t+1]`, ... against `gold[t]`, `gold[t+1]`, ...\n    -   Acceptance stops at the first mismatch.\n    -   Count accepted tokens per start position `t`.\n    -   Calculate metrics: `n_pos`, `n_draft_tokens`, `n_accepted`, `accept_rate`, `full_window_rate`, `mean_accepted_prefix`, `hist`.\n    -   Validation: lengths must match, `gamma >= 1`, lists non-empty.\n2.  `expected_tokens_per_step(alpha, gamma)` function.\n    -   Formula: `(1 - alpha**(gamma+1)) / (1 - alpha)` for `alpha != 1`.\n    -   Result `gamma + 1` for `alpha == 1`.\n    -   Validation: `alpha` in `[0, 1]`.\n3.  `__main__` block.\n    -   12-token example."
